  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Somalia Mobile Health Research Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Communities in about 70 rural villages around Jamaame town in southern Somalia have had little or no access to basic health services since 2007. Government services are non-existent and jihadists have gradually forced all foreign service providers to withdraw. The project will pilot a mobile clinic providing basic primary health care services and conduct a health needs assessment involving document review and local consultation with clinic and mobile service users and other organisations. The resulting report will be used to inform the new Mo Farah Foundation strategic plan and a project proposal for future long term work in the same project area.</narrative>
  </description>
